00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:15.749 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  i started visual communication at the  music poly  this was from 1993 to 95  the first 10 years of my career i was  really doing just graphic design  what i learned in school and then i  worked in advertising agencies  and soon after i started my own practice  asylum  the kind of projects that we started  working on a lot of it  is really for the retail industry for  fmv industry  and you know things that i really love  and as  i was designing the branding and  different visual aspects of it  i felt that the space was really crucial  to a brand's perspective  so it's not really just you know the  logo or the website  and hence from then onwards we started  to look at a more holistic approach  when it comes to design  [Music]  one of the earliest projects that we  started working on was a brand called  frolic  and this is a frozen yogurt brand and as  we were thinking  of you know different directions of how  we bring this brand to life  we looked at visual cues and we looked  at how  the the shop experience should be fun so  we took the opportunity of kind of  looking  at just purely graphic design to working  on the more holistic approach in looking  at interior design  looking at the digital experience so  from that small little project we kind  of  grew bolder and then slowly i guess we  got more opportunity  our biggest break was in shanghai where  we won the project to do sony gallery  which is a purely interior design  project  we had not much of an experience but we  took on the challenge  and we worked with an architect from  america and we collaborated hence we  kind of  learned hands on how do you work on a  proper interior space  i guess designers today could  collaborate a lot more  than the past because the projects tend  to be multifaceted  and they're just a lot more complicated  so you either  collaborate with partners that you can  work with  or you expand your kind of team so that  you can tackle  a lot more disciplines within one  project  [Music]  before i went on to the school of design  i  was think i was i just wanted to design  cd covers i thought i love  music and i look at album covers and wow  this is a great  career i could do that by going to the  school of design i'm exposed to  different disciplines like architecture  like photographers it really opened up  a big door for me to explore and which  is why i guess when i started  my career i did not want to be kind of  you know  pigeon hole into a certain discipline or  category  i get inspired by fashion designers i  get inspired by architects  i get inspired by you know artists  if you are 20 years old you should just  go and do whatever you want  you shouldn't be so fixated at what you  learn rather what you have  learned is the foundation where you can  really break free  don't be afraid of failure don't be  afraid of changing  just really explore but i think once you  find that love then you know dive  right into it

